  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice. \rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than six residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate surrounding",
    "No cooking facilities, including hot plates, shall be installed in the bedrooms of the development hereby permitted unless details have first been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Any cooking facilities shall thereafter only be implemented in accordance with the details that have been approved pursuant to this condition.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area",
    "Within three months, a detailed Fire Safety Strategy shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The strategy shall specifically address the means of escape for Bedroom 3 at ground floor level and shall include details of the escape route to a place of safety, including arrangements for any external gates, doors or enclosures, emergency lighting, and fire detection and alarm systems. The development shall thereafter be implemented and maintained in accordance with the approved strategy for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development provides an adequate means of escape for all occupants in the event of a fire and to comply with Policy D12 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "Within six months, waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the permitted number of occupiers shall be provided on site, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities are to be retained thereafter, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r \rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets",
    "Within six months, six long stay cycle parking spaces to satisfy the permitted number of occupiers on site shall be fully provided.\r \rThe dedicated cycle store providing six long stay parking spaces shall fulfil the following criteria:\r \rLocation: Near entrances or main access, \rDesign: Stands, \rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit, \rFully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof, \rAccessibility: 1.2m wide, Step-free, no obstructions.\r\rCycle parking shall be retained on site thereafter, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r \rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport"
  ],
